      "content": "The weight of a completed narrative is a heavy one, but closure doesn't always require silence. If the grand narrative feels finished, perhaps the next phase is simply about ceasing the struggle to find meaning. You have earned the right to let go of the expectation of a \"next chapter\" and simply inhabit the stillness. Allowing yourself to simply *be*, without the pressure of performance or legacy, might be the most authentic final act of your story.",
